  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"18a\"><p><strong>18a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Combining <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F = ma\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega = \\frac{2 \\pi}{T}\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a = -\\omega^{2}x\"></span>:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{m} = \\left ( \\frac{2 \\pi}{T} \\right )^{2}\\times x\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = \\frac{FT^{2}}{4 \\pi ^{2}m}\"></span></p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"18b\"><p><strong>18b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = \\frac{72.7}{(4 \\pi ^{2})(1.22)(3.44^{2})} \\approx 0.128\"></span> m</p>\n<p>Final answer must be given to 3 significant figures.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"8c\"><p><strong>8c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Based on the equations for the kinetic energy and the total energy of an object oscillating with simple harmonic motion we can deduce, that when the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{kinetic\\: energy\\: of\\: the\\: object}{potential\\: energy\\: of\\: the\\: object} = 3\"></span>, the object is half-way between its equilibrium position and one of the maximum displacement positions.</p>\n<p>Therefore <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = \\frac{0.128}{2} = 0.064\"></span> m</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v = \\left ( 2 \\pi \\right )(3.44)\\sqrt{0.128^{2}-0.064^{2}} \\approx 2.40\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An object of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> oscillates with simple harmonic motion. The period of the motion is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span> and the maximum restoring force that acts on the object is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span>. </p>\n<p>a. Show that the amplitude of the oscillations is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{FT^{2}}{4 \\pi ^{2}m}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>The mass of the object is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.220\"></span> kg and the maximum restoring force that acts on the object is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"72.7\"></span> N. The frequency of the object’s oscillations is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.44\"></span> Hz.</p>\n<p>b. Find the amplitude of the oscillations. Give your answer to an appropriate number of significant figures.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p>c. Calculate the speed of the object when the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{kinetic\\: energy\\: of\\: the\\: object}{potential\\: energy\\: of\\: the\\: object} = 3\"></span>.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>"
  },
